# Synchronicity product vision

Build a browser-automation product in the spirit of [browser-use.com](https://browser-use.com/): marketing pages plus a live agent-driven browser workspace.

## Product surfaces

- **Marketing**: landing / info pages now; pricing later (do not build pricing until requested)
- **App**: dashboard + live browser automation workspace (primary product)
- Keep marketing and app surfaces separate in architecture

## Core UX

- Split layout ~**80% browser / 20% chat** (browser left, prompt chat right)
- User prompts in the chat drive an agent that acts in the left-side browser
- Screenshots are sent to the model so it can monitor page state and choose actions

## Agent + browser behavior

- **Playwright** drives the real browser
- **OpenAI Agents JS** (`@openai/agents`) runs the agent loop: screenshot -> decide -> act
- Prefer SDK **`computerTool` + `Computer`** wired to Playwright: screenshot, click(x,y), doubleClick, scroll, type, keypress, move, wait, drag
- Prefer screenshot + coordinate tools over brittle CSS-selector-only automation

## Human-in-the-loop

- For login / auth / other sensitive flows: agent **pauses and requests user permission**
- User takes temporary control of the browser
- User presses **Continue** to resume from the **same / current step** (no restart from scratch)
- Treat user approval / handoff as a first-class agent state, not an afterthought
